    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug! The issue was in how the `frai` CLI was passing the `--ci` flag to the `frai-gate` command.\n\n**The Problem:**\nWhen running `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js was parsing the `--ci` flag as an option on the main `frai` program (since it was defined there), rather than passing it as an argument to the `gate` subcommand. This meant the `args` array received by the gate action handler only contained `['init']`, without the `--ci` flag.\n\n**The Fix:**\nI modified the gate command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Get the parsed options from the main program using `program.opts()`\n2. Check if the `--ci` flag was set\n3. Include it in the arguments passed to the `frai-gate` CLI\n\n**Verification:**\n- Built the updated `frai` CLI\n- Tested `frai gate init --ci` and confirmed that `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` is now created\n- The workflow file contains the correct GitHub Actions workflow configuration\n\nThe fix is minimal and focused only on passing through the `--ci` flag, as required.",
